# Manual API checks. Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
# (or JetBrains HTTP Client) and click "Send Request" above each block.
# Start the API first: `pnpm dev` from the repo root.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### Unknown route → 404
GET {{api}}/nope

### Plain-text email (JSON) → 200, open data.previewUrl
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "alice@example.com, bob@example.com",
  "cc": "carol@example.com",
  "bcc": "dave@example.com",
  "subject": "Hello from Email Composer",
  "body": "This is a plain-text email."
}

### HTML email (JSON) → 200 (a plain-text part is generated too)
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "alice@example.com",
  "subject": "HTML email",
  "body": "<h1>Hello</h1><p>This is <strong>HTML</strong> with a <a href=\"https://example.com\">link</a>.</p>",
  "isHtml": true
}

### Recipient normalisation → 200, 4 unique recipients
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": ["Alice@Example.com; alice@example.com", "bob@example.com"],
  "cc": "BOB@example.com, carol@example.com",
  "bcc": "carol@example.com, dave@example.com",
  "subject": "Dedupe test",
  "body": "Each person gets this once."
}

### Multipart with an attachment → 200
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="to"

alice@example.com
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="subject"

With attachment
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="body"

See the attached file.
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="attachments"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

These are my notes.
--BOUNDARY--

### Disallowed file type → 415
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="to"

alice@example.com
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="subject"

Bad attachment
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="body"

This should be rejected.
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="attachments"; filename="setup.exe"
Content-Type: application/x-msdownload

MZ
--BOUNDARY--

### Everything missing → 400 with per-field errors
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Invalid addresses → 400 naming each bad address
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "alice@example.com, bob@",
  "cc": "not-an-email",
  "subject": "Bad recipients",
  "body": "x"
}

### Header injection attempt → 400
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "alice@example.com",
  "subject": "Hi\r\nBcc: victim@example.com",
  "body": "x"
}

### Malformed JSON → 400
POST {{api}}/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{bad json
